commit 35ad609a44f69b9ec9f0f27bb4cce4b76d09d3f0
Author:     welpy-cw <h.w.forms@arcor.de>
AuthorDate: Thu Jul 9 21:29:38 2026 +0000
Commit:     jtracey@thunderbird.net <jtracey@thunderbird.net>
CommitDate: Thu Jul 9 21:31:49 2026 +0000

    Bug 1999348 - Honor block exceptions when global "Allow remote content" is enabled. r=mkmelin

    When the preference "mailnews.message_display.disable_remote_image" is
    false (i.e., remote content is globally allowed), the content policy's
    ShouldLoad method was immediately accepting all remote content without
    consulting the permission manager for DENY_ACTION (block) exceptions.
    This meant users who had globally allowed remote content could not
    selectively block it for specific senders or image hosts.

    This patch:

    1. Adds CheckRemoteContentPermissionForSender(), a single helper that
       replaces the near-identical ShouldAcceptRemoteContentForSender() and
       the new block-exception check. It takes a permission value
       (ALLOW_ACTION / DENY_ACTION) so both allow-list and block-list
       lookups share the same email-extraction and permission-manager logic.

    2. Modifies the !mBlockRemoteImages early-return path in ShouldLoad()
       to check both content-location and sender permissions for
       DENY_ACTION before accepting. If a block exception is found, the
       content is rejected and the user is notified via the existing
       remote-content-blocked notification.

    3. Adds a browser test (browser_blockException.js) covering:
       - Block exception for a sender when global allow is on
       - No block exceptions when global allow is on (sanity check)
       - Block exception for a content URL when global allow is on

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310313

